{"ticker":"CARRARO","symbol":"CARRARO","instrumentId":3193628,"name":"Carraro India","industry":"NSE-Auto/Truck-Original Eqp","about":"Carraro India, part of the Carraro Group, is a technology-driven, integrated supplier of axles, transmission systems, and gears for agricultural tractors, construction vehicles, and off-highway equipment. The company provides end-to-end solutions, including in-house product design and manufacturing, catering to OEMs across India. Its diverse portfolio includes axles and transmissions of various horsepower ranges, along with gears, shafts, and ring gears for industrial and automotive markets. Carraro India also offers spare parts for agricultural tractors and construction vehicles. Known for delivering mission-critical components, the company supports industries such as backhoe loaders, soil compactors, cranes, and concrete mixers, ensuring reliability and performance.","website":"www.carraroindia.com","location":null,"exchange":"NSE","fetchedAt":"2026-11-20T13:11:38.182Z","basis":"consolidated","price":{"value":468.8,"changePct":-0.6884863891536913,"week52High":608.5,"week52Low":423.1},"stats":[{"label":"Market capitalization","value":"₹2,665 Cr"},{"label":"Sales","value":"₹2,417 Cr"},{"label":"Shares in float","value":"17,624,000"},{"label":"No. of funds","value":"36"},{"label":"Shares held by funds","value":"9,602,211"},{"label":"Dividend yield","value":"1.44%"},{"label":"Book value","value":"4.72"},{"label":"U/D vol ratio","value":"1.1"},{"label":"LTDebt / equity","value":"19.0%"},{"label":"Alpha","value":"-0.03"},{"label":"Beta","value":"1.35"},{"label":"EPS growth rate","value":"80%"},{"label":"P/E ratio","value":"19.57"},{"label":"5-year P/E range","value":"23–46"},{"label":"Return on equity","value":"23.1%"},{"label":"Cash flow (INR)","value":"23.67"},{"label":"Volume","value":"45,738"},{"label":"Avg volume (50d)","value":"98,807"},{"label":"Master score","value":"49"},{"label":"EPS rating","value":"82"},{"label":"Price streng